<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-Feb sugar, coffee, cocoa imports fall.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-Feb sugar, coffee, cocoa imports fall.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian January-February imports of coffee, cocoa and raw sugar from outside the Commonwealth of Independent States fell year-on-year, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>The committee, quoted by Interfax news agency, said January-February non-CIS raw sugar imports slumped to around a quarter of year-ago levels, to 66,100 tonnes from 241,700 tonnes.</p>
<p>White sugar imports from all destinations plunged 53 percent to 136,300 tonnes from 288,300 tonnes in the same year-ago period.</p>
<p>Cocoa imports fell 10 percent to 11,000 tonnes and coffee imports slumped 43 percent to 2,800 tonnes.</p>
<p>The committee gave the following data --</p>
<p>RUSSIAN NON-CIS SUGAR, COFFEE, COCOA IMPORTS (THOUSAND TONNES)</p>
<p>					 Jan-Feb 1997	  Jan-Feb 1996</p>
<p>Raw sugar				66.1		    241.7</p>
<p> White sugar(all destinations)  136.3		    288.3</p>
<p> Coffee				   2.8			4.9</p>
<p> Cocoa				   11.0		     12.2</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
